menu "PECD Smart Plant"

choice SMART_PLANT_OPERATING_MODE
    prompt "Operating mode"
    default SMART_PLANT_MODE_BASELINE
    help
        BASELINE is the deliberately unoptimized experimental reference.
        OPTIMIZED uses timer deep sleep between fixed sensor samples and wakes
        the Raspberry Pi after a retained cycle count. Both modes use the same
        sensors, rules, calibration and serial protocol.

config SMART_PLANT_MODE_BASELINE
    bool "BASELINE - fixed twenty-second sampling"
    help
        Read both sensors every twenty seconds and transmit every sample. No
        adaptive sampling, automatic light sleep, or deep sleep is enabled by
        the application.

config SMART_PLANT_MODE_OPTIMIZED
    bool "OPTIMIZED - 20-second deep-sleep sensing and Pi wake"
    help
        Read both physical sensors once, retain the cycle state in RTC memory,
        and use timer deep sleep between samples. GPIO26 wakes the Raspberry
        Pi after a configured number of samples or a new environmental alarm.

endchoice

config SMART_PLANT_BUZZER_GPIO
    int "Passive buzzer signal GPIO"
    range 0 39
    default 25

config SMART_PLANT_DHT11_GPIO
    int "DHT11 data GPIO"
    range 0 33
    default 4
    help
        DHT11 needs a GPIO that supports both input and output. This project
        uses GPIO4.

config SMART_PLANT_SOIL_DRY_RAW
    int "Measured raw ADC value for the dry reference"
    range 0 4095
    default 0
    help
        Enter the averaged GPIO34 raw value measured with the probe in the
        chosen dry reference. Zero is a placeholder until calibration.

config SMART_PLANT_SOIL_WET_RAW
    int "Measured raw ADC value for the wet reference"
    range 0 4095
    default 0
    help
        Enter the averaged GPIO34 raw value measured with the probe in the
        chosen wet reference. Zero is a placeholder until calibration.

config SMART_PLANT_SOIL_CALIBRATED
    bool "Dry and wet soil ADC values were physically measured"
    default n
    help
        Enable only after both endpoints above have been measured on this
        exact sensor. Until then, normalized soil values and soil alerts are
        disabled; raw ADC diagnostics remain available.

config SMART_PLANT_OPTIMIZED_MIN_INTERVAL_S
    int "OPTIMIZED deep-sleep sampling interval (seconds)"
    range 10 3600
    default 20
    depends on SMART_PLANT_MODE_OPTIMIZED
    help
        The ESP32 remains awake only long enough to read the DHT11 and ADC,
        write its UART record, then sleeps for this timer interval. Twenty
        seconds is the reference scenario cadence.

config SMART_PLANT_OPTIMIZED_PI_NORMAL_CYCLES
    int "Normal camera interval and stable qualification (sensor cycles)"
    range 1 360
    default 90
    depends on SMART_PLANT_MODE_OPTIMIZED
    help
        Normally request camera analysis every 90 cycles (about 30 minutes).
        After this many consecutive valid alarm-free samples, use the stable interval.

config SMART_PLANT_OPTIMIZED_PI_WAKE_CYCLES
    int "Stable camera interval (sensor cycles)"
    range 1 360
    default 360
    depends on SMART_PLANT_MODE_OPTIMIZED
    help
        GPIO26 is pulsed at this stable interval, or sooner on alarm/fault.
        With the default twenty-second interval and 360 cycles, the Raspberry Pi
        is requested after 360 real sensor measurements (approximately two
        hours plus awake overhead; the cycle count is authoritative).

config SMART_PLANT_ALERT_COOLDOWN_S
    int "Repeated alert cooldown (seconds)"
    range 10 86400
    default 300
    help
        An active rule alerts on its inactive-to-active transition and then no
        more often than this cooldown while the condition remains active.

config SMART_PLANT_PI_WAKE_COOLDOWN_S
    int "Minimum time between Raspberry Pi wake pulses (seconds)"
    range 1 3600
    default 1
    depends on SMART_PLANT_MODE_OPTIMIZED
    help
        GPIO26 wakes a halted Raspberry Pi on policy requests. Limit pulses defensively in case of an unexpected reset.

endmenu
